---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import PlaceholderBox from "../components/PlaceholderBox.astro";
import StatusBadge from "../components/StatusBadge.astro";
import { reportedResults } from "../data/reportedResults";
import { href } from "../site.config";

const headlineRows = reportedResults.flatMap((group) =>
  group.rows.filter((row) => row.headline),
);
const detailGroups = reportedResults
  .map((group) => ({ ...group, rows: group.rows.filter((row) => !row.headline) }))
  .filter((group) => group.rows.length > 0);
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Research"
  description="Summary of the final-year project report and the status of the research paper. No report PDF and no paper text are published here."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Research"
    intro="A summary of the final-year project report. The report PDF is not published here. The research paper is under review, and nothing from it is published here."
  />
  <div class="container">
    <h2>Final-year project report</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>AI-Driven Honeybee and Beehive Health Monitoring System for Disease Detection and
      Population Analysis.</strong> Final-year project report, BSc Computer Science, Department of
      Computer Science, Namal University, cohort 2021–2025. Thirteen chapters plus references.
    </p>
    <p>What the report covers, in brief:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Problem and objectives</strong> (Chapter 1): colony decline, limits of manual inspection, and targets for image-based monitoring.</li>
      <li><strong>Literature</strong> (Chapter 2): prior work on bee detection, disease imaging, and counting. Figures in this chapter belong to other researchers, not to this project.</li>
      <li><strong>Method</strong> (Chapter 4): three-part framework, preprocessing, two MobileNet models, and a counting approach.</li>
      <li><strong>Results and discussion</strong> (Chapters 5–6): several metric sets that do not agree with each other, plus limits that qualify every result. Reported figures are published with sources in the section below.</li>
      <li><strong>System design, data, and testing</strong> (Chapters 7–11): prototype design, data sources, and small-scale testing including a small expert check.</li>
      <li><strong>Conclusions and future work</strong> (Chapters 12–13): summary and planned extensions, including a mobile app and pilot programmes.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      No report diagrams or images are republished here. The report's figures are diagrams, one
      bee-counting image, and two interface screenshots. Rights and permissions for reuse have
      not been confirmed.
    </p>
    <PlaceholderBox text="decision on publishing a redacted report copy (student IDs removed) with co-author and university permission — summary only for now" />

    <h2>Reported project results (from the final report and poster)</h2>
    <p>
      Reported by the project team. Independent measurement of the deployed demo models is pending.
    </p>
    <p>
      The figures below describe the project as reported in the final-year project report and on
      the project poster. Each figure carries its exact source and what it measures. The report's
      chapters disagree with each other on several measures, so the sets are shown separately and
      are never merged into one headline figure. None of these figures describes the two demo
      models on the <a href={href("/models-data")}>Models &amp; data</a> page: no report metric is
      tied to the supplied model files by name, and the demo models have not been measured yet.
    </p>
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        <strong>Withheld values.</strong> Three values from the report and poster are not shown
        here, because they also appear in the report's literature review as other researchers'
        results. They stay withheld until the project lead confirms in writing that each was
        independently measured in this project and on which test set. No processing-time figures
        are published, and no counting-model version number is shown.
      </p>
    </div>
    <h3>Headline: the most conservative independently tested figures</h3>
    <p>
      These figures come from Chapter 11 prototype testing: new images, cross-validation, and
      checks against expert assessment. Each carries its exact source and what it measures.
    </p>
    <div class="table-wrap">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr><th>Figure</th><th>Value</th><th>What it measures</th><th>Source</th></tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {headlineRows.map((row) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{row.figure}</td>
              <td><strong>{row.value}</strong></td>
              <td>{row.measures}</td>
              <td>{row.source}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <h3>All other reported figures, by chapter</h3>
    <p class="small muted">
      The remaining figures are grouped by chapter. Open a section to see its table.
    </p>
    {detailGroups.map((group) => (
      <details>
        <summary>{group.group}</summary>
        {group.note && <p class="small muted">{group.note}</p>}
        <div class="table-wrap">
          <table>
            <thead>
              <tr><th>Figure</th><th>Value</th><th>What it measures</th><th>Source</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {group.rows.map((row) => (
                <tr>
                  <td>{row.figure}</td>
                  <td><strong>{row.value}</strong></td>
                  <td>{row.measures}</td>
                  <td>{row.source}</td>
                </tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
      </details>
    ))}

    <h2>Research paper</h2>
    <p><StatusBadge kind="pending" label="Under review" /></p>
    <p>
      Status only: <strong>under review</strong>. No title, abstract, figures, or unpublished
      results are shown, and no journal is named, until the team supplies the details and confirms
      the journal's sharing policy.
    </p>
    <PlaceholderBox text="paper title, journal, submission date, and journal preprint/sharing policy, as confirmed by the team" />

    <h2>How this site uses the report</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Facts are tied to report sections. Targets are labelled as targets. Literature figures are never presented as project results.</li>
      <li>Where report chapters disagree, the site says so instead of picking one number silently. See <a href={href("/models-data")}>Models &amp; data</a>.</li>
      <li>Claims from outside the report (field work, awards, paper status) are labelled as team statements, with certificates and photos still to be added.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <a href={href("/project")}>Project summary</a> ·
      <a href={href("/team")}>Team and supervisors</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
